# Let the session read the controller's touchpad.
#
# It is an ordinary input device owned by root, so nothing running as the
# person using the machine can open it. The usual answer is the uaccess tag,
# which asks logind to hand a seat's devices to whoever is logged in; the tag
# is set here and on the device, and logind does not act on it for this one.
# So the permission is granted outright instead. This machine has one person
# on it, and the manifest already names them as the owner of everything else.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="*Legion Controller*Touchpad*", \
  TAG+="uaccess", RUN+="/usr/bin/setfacl -m u:player:rw /dev/input/%k"
